  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring Access to Emergency and Essential Health Services for Afghan Returnees, Refugees, Underserved Migrant Populations and Host Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to ensure the continuity of essential healthcare and post-arrival assistance by filling gaps in access to essential health services for those living in settlements underserved by health actors or with overburdened health facilities. To achieve this, IOM will strengthen coordination, provide essential health care, risk communication and community engagement, and border-level surveillance through six mobile health teams and rapid response teams to Herat, Nimroz3, Kandahar, Nangarhar, Balkh and Badakhshan. IOM will increase knowledge of population flows, returns, displacement and migration through the implementation of IOM&apos;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) to ensure better-targeted, evidence-based delivery of assistance to populations in most need in priority locations. DTM&apos;s activities will be nationwide, as they influence future geographical targeting of programs. Through the cross-border return and reintegration programme, IOM will provide humanitarian post-arrival assistance. Vulnerability screening, registration, health screening, refreshments and meals, temporary accommodation, transportation support, unconditional cash assistance, and onward referral for 5,000 returnees will be provided within the four major border crossing provinces. This project will also support the enhancement of the reception and transit center infrastructure to scale up capacity and operations to better meet the needs of the returnees.</narrative>
  </description>
